The table structure information is (table names): 
['player', 'team', 'match', 'player_match', 'ball_by_ball', 'batsman_scored', 'wicket_taken', 'extra_runs']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used

player.player_id : link every numeric id to the corresponding name  
player.player_name : final text we have to return  

ball_by_ball.match_id : joins every delivery to its match  
ball_by_ball.over_id / ball_id / innings_no : composite key to join with batsman_scored  
ball_by_ball.striker : the batsman (player_id) who faced the ball (used to accumulate runs)  
ball_by_ball.team_batting : the team the striker is representing in that ball (tells us whether that team finally won or lost)

batsman_scored.match_id / over_id / ball_id / innings_no : join‑columns that carry the number of runs actually credited to the striker on that ball  
batsman_scored.runs_scored : what we sum; we later keep only SUM >= 100  

match.match_id : join to the per‑match run table  
match.match_winner : team_id that finally won the match – if striker’s team_batting ≠ match_winner, that batsman’s team lost  


Typical conditions we will use
• SUM(batsman_scored.runs_scored) >= 100  
• team_batting <> match_winner                    -- team lost  
• match.match_winner IS NOT NULL                 -- ignore no‑result / tie if wanted  

Below are 10 exploratory/select‑statement only queries (all different, every one limited to 20 rows) that progressively build up to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at how runs are stored ball‑by‑ball
SELECT * 
FROM batsman_scored 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Bring in the striker who scored those runs
SELECT bb.match_id,
       bb.over_id,
       bb.ball_id,
       bb.striker      AS player_id,
       bs.runs_scored
FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
JOIN   ball_by_ball  AS bb
       ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
       AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
       AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
       AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Aggregate total runs per player per match
SELECT bb.match_id,
       bb.striker                    AS player_id,
       SUM(bs.runs_scored)           AS total_runs
FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
       ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
       AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
       AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
       AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Keep only 100‑plus knocks
SELECT bb.match_id,
       bb.striker                    AS player_id,
       SUM(bs.runs_scored)           AS total_runs
FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
       ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
       AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
       AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
       AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker
HAVING total_runs >= 100
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Add the batting team id for every 100+ effort
SELECT bb.match_id,
       bb.striker                    AS player_id,
       bb.team_batting               AS team_id,
       SUM(bs.runs_scored)           AS total_runs
FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
       ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
       AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
       AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
       AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker, bb.team_batting
HAVING total_runs >= 100
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Add match winner to see whether the scorer’s team lost or won
SELECT t.match_id,
       t.player_id,
       t.team_id,
       m.match_winner,
       t.total_runs
FROM (
        SELECT bb.match_id,
               bb.striker            AS player_id,
               bb.team_batting       AS team_id,
               SUM(bs.runs_scored)   AS total_runs
        FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
        JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
               ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
               AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
               AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
               AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
        GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker, bb.team_batting
        HAVING total_runs >= 100
     ) AS t
LEFT  JOIN match AS m
       ON m.match_id = t.match_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Filter to efforts made for the losing side
SELECT t.match_id,
       t.player_id,
       t.team_id,
       t.total_runs
FROM (
        SELECT bb.match_id,
               bb.striker            AS player_id,
               bb.team_batting       AS team_id,
               SUM(bs.runs_scored)   AS total_runs
        FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
        JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
               ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
               AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
               AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
               AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
        GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker, bb.team_batting
        HAVING total_runs >= 100
     ) AS t
JOIN match AS m
     ON m.match_id = t.match_id
WHERE t.team_id <> m.match_winner
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Attach player names to losing‑team centurions
SELECT p.player_name,
       x.total_runs,
       x.match_id
FROM (
        SELECT bb.match_id,
               bb.striker            AS player_id,
               bb.team_batting       AS team_id,
               SUM(bs.runs_scored)   AS total_runs
        FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
        JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
               ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
               AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
               AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
               AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
        GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker, bb.team_batting
        HAVING total_runs >= 100
     ) AS x
JOIN match  AS m  ON m.match_id  = x.match_id
JOIN player AS p  ON p.player_id = x.player_id
WHERE x.team_id <> m.match_winner
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as 8 but show the team names as well
SELECT DISTINCT
       p.player_name,
       t2.name                 AS team_name,
       x.total_runs,
       x.match_id
FROM (
        SELECT bb.match_id,
               bb.striker          AS player_id,
               bb.team_batting     AS team_id,
               SUM(bs.runs_scored) AS total_runs
        FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
        JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
               ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
               AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
               AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
               AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
        GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker, bb.team_batting
        HAVING total_runs >= 100
     ) AS x
JOIN match AS m   ON m.match_id  = x.match_id
JOIN team  AS t2  ON t2.team_id  = x.team_id
JOIN player AS p  ON p.player_id = x.player_id
WHERE x.team_id <> m.match_winner
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query – return just the distinct player names who hit ≥100
--     yet ended up on the losing side in that match
SELECT DISTINCT
       p.player_name
FROM (
        SELECT bb.match_id,
               bb.striker          AS player_id,
               bb.team_batting     AS team_id,
               SUM(bs.runs_scored) AS total_runs
        FROM   batsman_scored AS bs
        JOIN   ball_by_ball   AS bb
               ON  bb.match_id     = bs.match_id
               AND bb.over_id      = bs.over_id
               AND bb.ball_id      = bs.ball_id
               AND bb.innings_no   = bs.innings_no
        GROUP  BY bb.match_id, bb.striker, bb.team_batting
        HAVING total_runs >= 100
     ) AS x
JOIN match  AS m  ON m.match_id  = x.match_id
JOIN player AS p  ON p.player_id = x.player_id
WHERE x.team_id <> m.match_winner
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query (No. 10) yields the required list of players who scored at least 100 runs yet were on the losing side in that match.
